        <section id="integrated-processing">
            <div class="content-container">
                <h2>Integrated Cast, Forge, Machine, Finish and Inspect Programs</h2>
                <ol>
                    <li><strong>Review the drawing:</strong> confirm finish specification, masking, dimensions, appearance, and test requirements.</li>
                    <li><strong>Select the source:</strong> verify material compatibility, process capability, certification scope, capacity, and approvals.</li>
                    <li><strong>Plan machining allowance:</strong> account for buildup, penetration, removal, post-finish machining, and final inspection.</li>
                    <li><strong>Prepare and finish:</strong> clean, pretreat, mask, process, rinse, cure, seal, and handle according to the approved route.</li>
                    <li><strong>Inspect and document:</strong> verify coating, dimensions, performance, traceability, packaging, and shipment records.</li>
                </ol>
                <p>
                    Surface finishing can be coordinated with
                    <a href="/secondary-operations" class="highlight-link">secondary operations</a>,
                    <a href="/assembly-and-kitting" class="highlight-link">assembly and kitting</a>,
                    and
                    <a href="/quality-assurance-certifications" class="highlight-link">quality assurance</a>
                    according to the project scope.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

